Bound the HTTP/2 receive windows of the xhttp client.

Base: github.com/XTLS/Xray-core 50231eaff98c (v26.7.11), the commit libXray
v1.260711.0 pins as v1.260327.1-0.20260711155151-50231eaff98c. Applied by
scripts/build-cores-ios.sh on a clone of that commit before the bind.

x/net/http2 gives every stream a 4 MB receive window and every connection
1 GB, and exposes neither on http2.Transport; it reads them only from a
net/http.Transport's HTTP2 config. On an iOS packet tunnel provider, killed
at about 50 MB, that per-stream window is the buffer that fills when the tun
path drains slower than the link: the 1.0.424 trace lost 15 MB of live heap
to it in five seconds of a speed test's download. Two env flags, read the
way Xray reads its other knobs (platform.EnvFlag), bound them:

  xray.xhttp.h2.stream.window  /  XRAY_XHTTP_H2_STREAM_WINDOW   bytes per stream
  xray.xhttp.h2.conn.window    /  XRAY_XHTTP_H2_CONN_WINDOW     bytes per connection

Unset or non-positive keeps x/net's defaults, so nothing changes for anyone
who does not set them.

